@startuml 01_User_Signup

title 01. User Signup - Generate Identity Secret

actor User
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "Device Storage" as Storage
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB

User -> Client: Register (email, password)
activate Client

Client -> Server: POST /auth/register\n{email, password}
activate Server

Server -> DB: Create user account
activate DB
DB --> Server: User created
deactivate DB

Server --> Client: 201 Created\n{user_id, session_token}
deactivate Server

Client -> Crypto: Generate identity secret
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  Generate 256-bit random key
  using crypto.getRandomValues()
  (CSPRNG)
end note

Crypto -> Crypto: Generate identity_secret\n(32 bytes, high entropy)
Crypto --> Client: identity_secret
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Storage: Store identity_secret
activate Storage
note right of Storage
  Stored securely on device
  NEVER transmitted to server
  NEVER leaves the device
end note
Storage --> Client: Stored successfully
deactivate Storage

Client --> User: Registration complete\n⚠️ "Save recovery method"
deactivate Client

note over User, DB
  At this point:
  ✅ User account created on server
  ✅ Identity secret generated CLIENT-SIDE
  ✅ Identity secret stored on device
  ❌ Server has NO knowledge of identity secret
end note

@enduml
